# A trailer-only model with formals (T7-TRAILER-ONLY-MODEL-CRASH).  add has no body but its return; it reads
# y, x and other, a field of the unit.  wrap returns merge(y: k; add): the node walks the trailer alone, with
# y bound and x given, and other read from the copy of the unit made at the merge.  prep wrote 9 before the
# merge; bump writes 11 after it.  w's copy reads 9 before and after bump: 5 + 1 + 9; the original add, called
# by orig after bump, reads 11: 5 + 1 + 11.  The root calls are above the unit's declaration of other: no
# caller binding reaches them.  Entry 7.
int: z0 prep()
@: w wrap(5)
int: a1 (plain())
int: z1 bump()
int: a2 (plain())
int: o (orig())
int: other 9

fn: add (int: y; int: x) int
return: y + x + other

fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x) int
    return: merge(y: k; add)

fn: plain () int
    return: (w: 1)
end: plain

fn: orig () int
    return: add(5 1)
end: orig

fn: prep () int
    node\other: 9
    return: 0
end: prep

fn: bump () int
    node\other: 11
    return: 0
end: bump

int: ok 81
if: a1 = 15 && a2 = 15 && o = 17
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
